-- title:
--   Integral (ζ'-1)-divisible difference of Tate toric x-series
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$. Fix a natural number $N$ and units $c,\zeta'$ of $A$ such that $1-c$ and $1-\zeta' c$ are units of $A$. The assertion is the existence of a power series $P\in A[\![X]\!]$ such that (i) every coefficient $\operatorname{coeff}_n P$ lies in the ideal of $A$ generated by $\zeta'-1$, and (ii) after base change along $A\to L$, the Laurent (Hahn) series $\mathrm{ofPowerSeries}$ of $P$ mapped into $L[\![X]\!]$ equals the difference of the first components of $\mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,L\,N$ evaluated at the images in $L^{\times}$ of $\zeta' c$ and of $c$. Here the first component of $\mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,R\,p\,d$ is the Hahn series attached to the power series whose $m$-th coefficient is $d\cdot\mathrm{Ring.inverse}(1-d)^{2}$ for $m=0$ and, for $m\ge 1$, $\sum_{e\mid m,\ p\mid e}(m/e)\,(d^{m/e}+d^{-m/e})-2\,[\,p\mid m\,]\sum_{e\mid m/p}e$. No primality or nonvanishing condition is imposed on $N$.
--
--   This is the integrality and congruence statement for the difference of the $x$-coordinates of two toric points on a Tate curve, the $q$-expansion side of the comparison between the points parametrised by $c$ and by $\zeta' c$. It is used in the construction of level automorphisms near the cusps, where the difference must be shown to be integral and divisible by $\zeta'-1$ at the chosen place.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_powerSeries_forall_coeff_mem_span_sub_one_ofPowerSeries_eq_tateToricPoint_mul_sub_tateToricPoint.lean

